# udev rule — Framework Laptop 13 (AMD) suspend wakeup fix.
#
# Problem: the embedded controller on this mainboard emits spurious wake events —
# charger/USB-C power events fire a synthetic keyboard event that can wake the
# machine right after suspending and leave it awake (e.g. in a bag), draining the
# battery.
#
# Effect: disables wakeup for the AT keyboard controller (serio0). Opening the
# lid still wakes the machine on purpose — that is how it is normally resumed.
#
# Note (2026-10-14): the original version of this rule also targeted the ACPI lid
# switch (PNP0C0D) with `SUBSYSTEM=="acpi", DRIVERS=="button"`. On current
# kernels that match never fires — the lid device is `SUBSYSTEM=="platform"`,
# driver `acpi-button` — so the line was dead code and has been dropped
# (verified with `udevadm test`; the keyboard half applies correctly).
#
# Revert: remove this file and rebuild, or at runtime:
#   echo enabled > /sys/devices/platform/i8042/serio0/power/wakeup
# (values reset on reboot).
#
# References:
#   https://community.frame.work/t/tracking-framework-amd-ryzen-7040-series-lid-wakeup-behavior-feedback/39128

ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="serio", DRIVERS=="atkbd", ATTR{power/wakeup}="disabled"
